  "formulae": {
    "mu_m": "mean over K independently keyed N-pass linear RGB films for method m",
    "mu_pool": "equal-weight mean of mu_m over every required method in this condition",
    "D": "sum over all pixels and RGB channels of mu_pool squared",
    "V_m": "sum over all pixels and channels of sample variance (ddof=1) across K films, divided by D",
    "perPassProxy": "N * V_m",
    "cost": "median across K runs of 1000 * renderPassSeconds / measuredPasses",
    "varianceCostProxy": "N * V_m * cost",
    "estimatedTotalRenderingMs": "N * post-warmup median milliseconds/pass (warmup film samples are not free)",
    "meanEnergy": "mean over pixels of Rec.709 RGB luminance, then mean over seed runs",
    "energyRatio": "method meanEnergy / equal-weight pooled method meanEnergy"
  },
  "scope": [
    "Empirical seed-to-seed dispersion of this implementation. There is no ground-truth image in this analysis; these are not MSE measurements.",
    "The common normalization includes each tested method and is itself estimated. It permits within-condition comparison and cannot prove correct energy.",
    "Whole-frame RGB variance includes every pixel; no brightness-dependent mask or clipping is used in numerical analysis.",
    "N*variance assumes a per-pass scale only as a descriptive proxy. A finite run does not prove finite variance, asymptotic convergence or absence of bias.",
    "A small number of seed-key runs can miss rare singular events. Values and rankings are exploratory; no confidence intervals are claimed.",
    "The same key set is used across methods. Cross-method paired streams can be correlated; no independence assumption between methods is needed for each method variance.",
    "One pass draws one record per selected member (some members can have paired roots). A six-member pass is more work than a singleton pass.",
    "Native cost times the primary CPU renderPass only, after eight warmup passes; it excludes process initialization, UI, display, dumping and secondary films.",
    "Reported timing min/max is observed run spread, not a confidence interval. The GPU renderer string describes the display context, not a GPU implementation of the estimator.",
    "Each isolated source is centered at a common position. Full rooms also change position, overlap and source-selection probabilities; composite results cannot isolate those causes.",
    "All tested masks here are exact-sheet/directional combinations; this suite does not establish finite-radius curve bias or cross-group MIS behavior.",
    "Beauty images share one exposure and display transfer; numerical data precedes that transformation."
  ],
